FUN_00433ba0 @0x433ba0: the bowl-cars target list push is a BYTE store.

The surfai/bowl target queue @bowl_cars (0x78a364, popped bytewise by
AI_Com_Server -- patch 495 fixed the POP side) is FILLED with byte pushes:
  433be2: 40         inc %eax
  433bea: 88 50 ff   mov %dl,-0x1(%eax)     ; BYTE store, pointer stepped +1
The mechanical deref-cast pass (patch 005) rendered the push as
`*(int*)_DAT_0078a378 = ...` -- a 4-byte store advancing by 1: every push
zeroed the next three queue entries, so the list ended up mostly zeros
(ref holds packed car indices 13..19).  The AI then targeted car 0/garbage
instead of the intended bowl opponents -> physics diverged from the
reference at cf51 and cascaded into the first collision (cf55/56 fb split
of the L9 attract).  Fix: byte store, matching the asm.

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -23419,7 +23419,7 @@
       do {
         if ((*(int *)(&DAT_00792a92 + iVar6) == 0) && (*(int *)(&DAT_00792ac6 + iVar6) == 0)) {
           pcVar1 = _DAT_0078a378 + 1;
-          *(int*)_DAT_0078a378 = (char)iVar2 + '\x01';
+          *(char*)_DAT_0078a378 = (char)iVar2 + '\x01';  /* BYTE push (asm 0x433bea: mov %dl,-0x1(%eax)) */
           _DAT_0078a378 = pcVar1;
         }
         iVar2 = iVar2 + 1;
